Doctor: Let''s start with your diet. First, it''s necessary to examine what you eat every day.
Patient: Well, I love fried chicken and sugary drinks.
Doctor: I see. Cut out the fatty food and the sugary drinks, and eat more fruit and vegetables.
Patient: That sounds hard. I also sit at my desk all day.
Doctor: Then try to exercise regularly. Even a thirty-minute walk each day will help.
Patient: All right. I''ll change my diet and start walking.
Doctor: Good. Remember, it takes time, so change slowly and don''t give up.', '病人想减重却做不到;医生说先要检查每天吃什么;病人爱吃炸鸡和含糖饮料;医生让他戒掉油腻食物和含糖饮料、多吃果蔬;病人整天坐着;医生建议规律锻炼,每天散步30分钟;病人答应改饮食并开始散步;医生提醒要慢慢来、别放弃。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does the patient want to do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Lose weight.","Gain weight.","Learn to cook.","Change jobs."]},{"q":"What does the doctor want to check first?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["His sleep.","What he eats every day.","His phone use.","His marks at school."]},{"q":"What food does the patient say he loves?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Fried chicken and sugary drinks.","Fruit and vegetables.","Nuts and dried meat.","Rice and soup."]},{"q":"What exercise does the doctor suggest?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Lifting heavy weights.","A thirty-minute walk each day.","Swimming for an hour.","Playing computer games."]},{"q":"What does the doctor say about changing?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It must happen in one day.","It is impossible to do.","It takes time, so change slowly.","It needs a special pill."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U2');
Tom: Yeah. I stayed up late on my phone watching videos again.
Lily: I think the phone is the problem. It''s affecting your schoolwork.
Tom: I know. Whenever I feel bored, I just pick up my phone straight away.
Lily: So boredom is your cue. Why don''t you change the routine?
Tom: Have you got any ideas?
Lily: When you feel bored, take a short walk or read a few pages instead.
Tom: That''s a good idea. I''ll leave my phone in another room tonight.', 'Lily 说 Tom 又累了、没睡够;Tom 又熬夜看视频;Lily 认为手机是问题、影响功课;Tom 一无聊就立刻拿手机;Lily 指出无聊是他的提示,建议换常规;Tom 问有什么主意;Lily 建议无聊时去散步或读几页书;Tom 觉得是好主意,决定今晚把手机放别的房间。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why does Tom look tired?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He stayed up late on his phone.","He exercised too much.","He got up very early to study.","He was ill with the flu."]},{"q":"What does Lily think is the problem?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["His diet.","The phone.","His friends.","His homework load."]},{"q":"What is Tom''s cue for picking up the phone?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Feeling hungry.","Feeling sleepy.","Feeling bored.","Feeling cold."]},{"q":"What does Lily suggest doing instead?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Buying a new phone.","Watching more videos.","Sleeping all day.","Taking a walk or reading a few pages."]},{"q":"What will Tom do tonight?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Leave his phone in another room.","Watch videos longer.","Skip his homework.","Stay up even later."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U2');
Anna: Don''t worry. To change a habit slowly is easier than stopping all at once.
Sam: So what should I do first?
Anna: Drink one less can each week, and replace it with water.
Sam: That sounds possible. Anything else?
Anna: Give yourself a small reward when you reach a goal, like watching a comedy.
Sam: Good idea. And if I fail one day?
Anna: Don''t become pessimistic. Just start again the next day.', 'Sam 想戒掉喝太多可乐却做不到;Anna 说慢慢改比一下子戒掉更容易;Sam 问先做什么;Anna 建议每周少喝一罐、用水代替;Sam 觉得可行,问还有别的吗;Anna 建议达成目标就给自己小奖励,比如看部喜剧;Sam 问万一某天失败了;Anna 说别悲观,第二天重新开始就好。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What habit does Sam want to break?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Watching too much TV.","Sleeping too little.","Drinking too much cola.","Eating too much meat."]},{"q":"What does Anna say about changing a habit?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It must be done all at once.","It is impossible to change.","Only a doctor can help.","Changing slowly is easier than stopping suddenly."]},{"q":"What is Anna''s first piece of advice?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Drink one less can each week and replace it with water.","Stop drinking water.","Drink even more cola.","Buy a bigger bottle."]},{"q":"What reward does Anna suggest?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Eating sweets.","Watching a comedy.","Buying new cola.","Staying up late."]},{"q":"What should Sam do if he fails one day?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Give up completely.","Drink more cola than before.","Not become pessimistic and start again the next day.","Blame his friends."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U2');

-- ===== 6) 写作 1篇 =====
DELETE FROM public.junior_writing_prompts WHERE volume='elective3' AND unit='U2';

Thanks for your letter. I know exactly how you feel, because using a phone too much was once my problem too. Staying up late on the screen harms your sleep and leaves you tired all day, so it is wise to change this habit slowly.

Here is what helped me. Try to understand your habit cycle: boredom is the cue, and scrolling is the routine. To break this habit, keep the cue but choose a better routine, such as a short walk or a good book. To exercise regularly also keeps us fit and refreshed.

It takes willpower, but don''t give up. Small steps over time really work!

Yours,
Li Hua', '【15 分制】A 档(13-15):五要素齐全、组织有条理、语言准确多样;B 档(10-12):要点较全、少量错误;C 档(7-9):要点偏少、句型简单;D 档(0-6):内容不完整、错误多。', '["To exercise regularly keeps us fit and refreshed.","It is wise to change this bad habit slowly, one small step at a time.","To break this habit, keep the cue but choose a better routine.","It takes willpower, but don''t give up — small steps over time really work."]'::jsonb, '[{"wrong":"Exercise regularly keep us fit.","correct":"To exercise regularly keeps us fit.","note":"不定式作主语,谓语用单数 keeps;且作主语用 To exercise。"},{"wrong":"It is important eat a balanced diet.","correct":"It is important to eat a balanced diet.","note":"it 作形式主语,真正主语用不定式 to eat,不可漏 to。"},{"wrong":"It takes willpower quitting smoking.","correct":"It takes willpower to quit smoking.","note":"It takes + n. + to do 句式,真正主语用不定式 to quit。"}]'::jsonb, '【健康建议信结构】
称呼:Dear Chris,
第1段 理解+危害:I know how you feel … Using a phone too much harms your sleep and health.
第2段 方法(习惯循环):Understand your habit cycle … To break this habit, keep the cue but choose a better routine … To exercise regularly keeps us fit.
第3段 鼓励+落款:It takes willpower, but don''t give up. Yours, Li Hua', 2, 'elective3', 'U2');

